/* book Worked example: Q: Complete the design of the edge beam of the previous chapter at the section where Mu = 150 kN·m, Vu = 120 kN and Tu = 30 kN·m. b = 300 mm, D = 600 mm, d = 550 mm, M25, Fe415, nominal cover 30 mm, 10 mm stirrups.
   1. Mt = 30 × (1 + 600/300)/1.7 = 30 × 3/1.7 = 52.94 kN·m. Since Mt < Mu, no steel is needed for Me2.
   2. Me1 = 150 + 52.94 = 202.94 kN·m. Mu,lim = 0.138 × 25 × 300 × 550² = 313.1 kN·m, so the section is singly reinforced.
   3. Tension steel: 202.94 × 10⁶ = 0.87 × 415 × Ast × 550 × (1 − 415 Ast/(300 × 550 × 25)) gives Ast = 1157 mm². (Me1/(b d²) = 2.24 N/mm² and the SP 16 flexure table for M25 and Fe415 gives pt ≈ 0.70 %, the same answer.)
   4. Provide four 20 mm bars at the bottom: 1257 mm². Check: xu = 0.87 × 415 × 1257/(0.36 × 25 × 300) = 168 mm < xu,max = 0.48 × 550 = 264 mm, and MR = 0.87 × 415 × 1257 × (550 − 0.416 × 168) = 217.8 kN·m ≥ 202.94 kN·m.
   5. Top: two 12 mm corner bars (226 mm²) to hold the stirrups and act as torsion stringers.
   6. Side faces: D = 600 mm > 450 mm, so provide 0.1 % × 300 × 600 = 180 mm², that is one 12 mm bar on each face (113 mm² each) at mid-depth; the gaps are about 250 mm, below 300 mm.
   7. Shear and torsion (from the previous chapter): Ve = 280 kN, τve = 1.70 N/mm², τc = 0.57 N/mm²; closed 10 mm stirrups at 140 mm.
   8. Final section: 4 bars of 20 mm at the bottom, 2 of 12 mm at the top, 1 of 12 mm on each side face, 10 mm closed stirrups at 140 mm with 135° hooks.
   Answer: Me1 = 202.94 kN·m needs 1157 mm²: four 20 mm bars (1257 mm², MR = 217.8 kN·m). Two 12 mm top bars, one 12 mm bar on each side face, and 10 mm closed stirrups at 140 mm. */
