/* book Worked example 2: Q: Near the support of the same beam, Mu = 30 kN·m while Vu and Tu are still 120 kN and 30 kN·m. Is steel needed on the top face, and are the bars of worked example 1 enough there?
   1. Mt = 52.94 kN·m as before. Now Mt > Mu = 30 kN·m.
   2. Bottom face: Me1 = 30 + 52.94 = 82.94 kN·m, needing Ast = 437 mm². The four 20 mm bars (1257 mm²) continue to the support, so this is met.
   3. Top face: Me2 = 52.94 − 30 = 22.94 kN·m acting in the opposite sense, so the top face is in tension. Taking the top bars at an effective depth of 600 − 46 = 554 mm, the steel needed is 116 mm².
   4. The two 12 mm top bars give 226 mm² > 116 mm², so they are enough, but they are now tension bars: they must run continuously and be anchored into the support with full development length, not stopped as hanger bars.
   Answer: Yes: Mt = 52.94 > Mu = 30 kN·m, so Me2 = 22.94 kN·m needs 116 mm² on the top face. The two 12 mm top bars (226 mm²) are enough if they are continuous and fully anchored; the bottom face needs 437 mm² for Me1 = 82.94 kN·m. */
