/* book exam traps: Designing the bottom steel for Mu alone. The tension face is designed for Me1 = Mu + Mt. | Forgetting Me2 near supports or wherever Mu is small. When Mt > Mu, the top face is in tension and its bars must be designed and anchored as tension bars. | Designing the stirrups for Ve with the ordinary shear formula. With torsion, Asv comes from Tu sv/(b1 d1 0.87 fy) + Vu sv/(2.5 d1 0.87 fy), with Ve used only for τve and the lower limit. | Leaving out the side-face bars of a beam deeper than 450 mm under torsion. | Writing Mt = Tu (1 + b/D)/1.7. The ratio is D/b, overall depth over breadth: 2.0 here, not 0.5. */
