/* book exam traps: Using the plain-bar bond stress for deformed bars. For M25 deformed bars in tension τbd = 2.24 N/mm², not 1.4 N/mm²; using 1.4 makes Ld 1.6 times too long (1032 mm instead of 645 mm for a 16 mm bar). | Using fy instead of 0.87 fy for σs in tension. | Counting a hook towards Ld of a bar in compression. Only the straight projected length counts in compression. | Treating the support width as the available anchorage. The simple-support check is Ld ≤ 1.3 M1/V + L0, with L0 measured beyond the centre of the support. | Forgetting to increase Ld for bundled bars (10, 20 or 33 % for two, three or four bars). */
